WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.668 --> 00:00:03.335
 Nate, Richard,
congratulations.

00:00:03.435 --> 00:00:05.005
You guys have made it
into the final round

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:07.173
of this competition, which
means that you're both one

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:10.109
step closer to the title
of Forged in Fire champion

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:12.411
and a check for $10,000.

00:00:12.478 --> 00:00:14.213
Now, we're sending you
back to your home forges

00:00:14.313 --> 00:00:17.484
to recreate an iconic
weapon from history.

00:00:17.584 --> 00:00:23.723
That weapon is the kpinga.

00:00:23.823 --> 00:00:24.690
Good luck.

00:00:24.757 --> 00:00:25.792
We'll see you in five days.

00:00:30.029 --> 00:00:32.532
 I'm so excited to
be representing Texas.

00:00:32.599 --> 00:00:33.799
That really is big for me.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:35.067
I want to win this
for all of us.

00:00:35.168 --> 00:00:38.637
I stole modeling
clay from my kids,

00:00:38.737 --> 00:00:39.972
they're not going to be happy.

00:00:40.072 --> 00:00:42.308
So this crazy kpinga,
nobody makes these.

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:45.044
I think that my metallurgy
background is going to give

00:00:45.144 --> 00:00:47.147
me an advantage over Nate.

00:00:47.247 --> 00:00:50.215
I think I want to end up getting
a lot of length on the handle,

00:00:50.315 --> 00:00:52.051
bending this guy, bend this guy.

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:54.987
There's a kpinga in this
big old hunk of stuff.

00:00:55.054 --> 00:00:57.056
Any time you take
steel and you bend it.

00:00:57.156 --> 00:00:59.292
With every action,
there's a reaction.

00:00:59.392 --> 00:01:02.361
It's compressing on one side,
elongating another, lot of

00:01:02.461 --> 00:01:04.297
stress going into those joints.

00:01:04.364 --> 00:01:07.200
Nate is an awesome smith and I
know he's bringing his A game,

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:08.234
as well.

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:11.837 line:8%
Starting to take a
little bit more shape.

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:14.474
 I have shaped the
kpinga complete.

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:17.076
I have to do a lot
of grinding today.

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:20.380
I'm trying to get in
here, and in here.

00:01:20.447 --> 00:01:23.148
I can't get all the angles
that I want to because

00:01:23.215 --> 00:01:24.884
of the shape of the weapon.

00:01:24.951 --> 00:01:26.986
So I am taking
creative liberties

00:01:27.053 --> 00:01:30.256
in how to grind this kpinga.

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:31.424
Whoa!

00:01:31.491 --> 00:01:33.893
It's just a tricky
blade to grind.

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:37.730
Totally different from
the ordinary blades.

00:01:37.796 --> 00:01:40.299
Gotta be careful.

00:01:40.399 --> 00:01:44.404
Now, I have some very
fine art work to do.

00:01:44.471 --> 00:01:46.839
Understanding exactly the
texture that I want here

00:01:46.906 --> 00:01:51.944
is going to determine what
kind of chisel I need to use.

00:01:52.010 --> 00:01:54.180
Just heat this up a little bit.

00:01:54.247 --> 00:01:56.683
The technique I'm going
to be using for engraving

00:01:56.749 --> 00:01:58.484
is based on Japanese metal work.

00:01:58.550 --> 00:02:03.155
And they used pine tar to secure
their metal to a worktable.

00:02:03.256 --> 00:02:06.826
I don't have any pine
resin, so I used hot glue.

00:02:06.892 --> 00:02:08.661
This cannot be done well tense.

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:17.670
The patterns I've added to
this really give this piece

00:02:17.737 --> 00:02:19.672
more of historical accuracy.

00:02:19.739 --> 00:02:21.874
These are more than just
simple throwing knives.

00:02:21.941 --> 00:02:25.111
The Zandes believed that these
are symbols of warriorship

00:02:25.177 --> 00:02:26.746
and they were highly revered.

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:29.915
So I'm very proud that
the designs hand chiseled,

00:02:30.015 --> 00:02:31.450
think it looks spectacular.

00:02:31.517 --> 00:02:33.386 line:14%
Perfect.

00:02:33.486 --> 00:02:36.656 line:8%
 I'm really happy where
I'm at at this point.

00:02:36.756 --> 00:02:38.291
So it's time to heat treat.

00:02:38.357 --> 00:02:40.826
It may snap right here, there's
so many different areas.

00:02:40.926 --> 00:02:42.428
This is a long blade.

00:02:42.495 --> 00:02:44.130
I'm thinking, how am I
going to heat treat it?

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:48.100
I have to heat the whole
blade evenly, and then quench.

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:49.935
This is for $10,000.

00:02:50.002 --> 00:02:52.371
This has got to be right.

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:53.840
[bleep], it doesn't fit.

00:02:53.906 --> 00:02:57.643
If I can't get that blade
heated, it's not a blade.

00:02:57.710 --> 00:02:59.879
If I stuck it in there
like that and took

00:02:59.946 --> 00:03:02.215
the torch and heated that
guy at the same time,

00:03:02.281 --> 00:03:04.716
pull it off, boom.

00:03:04.817 --> 00:03:05.585
I can do that.

00:03:08.187 --> 00:03:10.522
So I have the bigger
blade in the forge.

00:03:10.622 --> 00:03:13.760
I'm heating up the part
that's sticking out.

00:03:13.826 --> 00:03:15.961
This is not ideal heat treating.

00:03:16.028 --> 00:03:17.529
This is not how I do things.

00:03:17.629 --> 00:03:19.699
I don't know if this
has ever even been done.

00:03:19.765 --> 00:03:21.467
If this works, it is
going to be a miracle.

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:22.302
Come on.

00:03:25.438 --> 00:03:27.206
I've got no other options.

00:03:27.306 --> 00:03:30.108
It's got to be done today.

00:03:30.175 --> 00:03:32.946
Hard, hard.

00:03:33.046 --> 00:03:34.012
All of it got hard.

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:35.314
I'm very happy.

00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:38.350 line:14%
I was wound up tight about this.

00:03:38.417 --> 00:03:41.187 line:8%
 I am feeling a little
urgency because I have

00:03:41.253 --> 00:03:42.722
three things to get done today.

00:03:42.788 --> 00:03:47.259
Heat treat the blade, put on
a handle, and then sharpen it.

00:03:47.359 --> 00:03:49.796
The heat treat goes swimmingly.

00:03:49.896 --> 00:03:51.296
There's no warping.

00:03:51.396 --> 00:03:53.332
So the handle, I'm going
to try out something

00:03:53.399 --> 00:03:55.134
I've never done before.

00:03:55.201 --> 00:03:56.836
I'm going to use a braid.

00:03:56.936 --> 00:04:00.072
I chose goatskin because
it's excellent for braiding,

00:04:00.138 --> 00:04:02.308
it's very strong and very thin.

00:04:02.375 --> 00:04:04.510
Got to love leather.

00:04:04.577 --> 00:04:06.044
The last thing I'm
adding to the handle

00:04:06.111 --> 00:04:07.880
is a wax called saddle soap.

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:10.049
Goop it on, wipe off the excess.

00:04:10.116 --> 00:04:12.051
This is just to
protect the leather,

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:16.455
and to give it a little bit
more of a comfortable grip.

00:04:16.555 --> 00:04:19.258
It's just so much
energy in the air

00:04:19.325 --> 00:04:21.026
that it actually
started to hail.

00:04:21.093 --> 00:04:22.361
I think this is a good omen.

00:04:22.461 --> 00:04:24.430
I'm bringing something
deadly into this world,

00:04:24.497 --> 00:04:26.399
this is the birth
of something great.

00:04:29.368 --> 00:04:30.603
 Bladesmiths, the kpinga.

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:32.672
It's made to be a
throwing weapon.

00:04:32.739 --> 00:04:35.141
With so much blade, I wonder
what kind of lethal damage

00:04:35.207 --> 00:04:36.308
it's going to do.

00:04:36.409 --> 00:04:37.676
Nate, you're up first.
You ready?

00:04:37.743 --> 00:04:38.544
 I'm ready.

00:04:43.649 --> 00:04:44.417
 Wow.

00:04:56.261 --> 00:04:57.462
 All right, Nate.

00:04:57.562 --> 00:05:00.332
It feels good when you throw it.

00:05:00.399 --> 00:05:03.335
The penetration of
your blade is so deep,

00:05:03.402 --> 00:05:05.805
that will hit vital organs.

00:05:05.905 --> 00:05:09.875
This is definitely the
back scratcher of death.

00:05:09.942 --> 00:05:13.746
This weapon will kill.

00:05:13.813 --> 00:05:14.680
Richard, you're next.

00:05:14.747 --> 00:05:15.247
You ready?

00:05:15.348 --> 00:05:16.316
 Let's do it.

00:05:20.819 --> 00:05:21.654
Awesome.

00:05:32.064 --> 00:05:34.467
Wow.

00:05:34.567 --> 00:05:37.236
 Well Richard, when
you throw it it's

00:05:37.303 --> 00:05:39.772
got good balance for
forward momentum.

00:05:39.839 --> 00:05:42.909
Enough to penetrate
into the carcass.

00:05:42.975 --> 00:05:45.912
Overall, your weapon will kill.

00:05:46.012 --> 00:05:46.612
Good job.

00:05:46.679 --> 00:05:47.980
 Thank you.

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:49.548
All right, gentlemen to test
the strength and durability

00:05:49.615 --> 00:05:52.084
of your kpingas, I'll be
throwing them into our log

00:05:52.184 --> 00:05:54.453
wall, three times each weapon.

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:55.988
Nate, you're up first.

00:06:23.082 --> 00:06:27.053
So Nate, your handle is
really beautifully done.

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:28.687
But it's sticky.

00:06:28.754 --> 00:06:29.788
 Yeah.

00:06:29.855 --> 00:06:32.324
 That first throw,
instead of releasing here,

00:06:32.391 --> 00:06:34.426
I released all
the way down here.

00:06:34.527 --> 00:06:37.295
And it just was
stuck in my hand.

00:06:37.396 --> 00:06:39.632
Having said that,
it buried itself

00:06:39.698 --> 00:06:41.033
in that wood quite beautifully.

00:06:41.133 --> 00:06:41.801
 OK.

00:06:41.868 --> 00:06:42.801
 Nicely done.

00:06:42.868 --> 00:06:43.836
 Thank you.

00:06:43.936 --> 00:06:44.336
 All right, Richard.

00:06:44.437 --> 00:06:46.072
 Let's do it.

00:07:00.586 --> 00:07:02.121
 I'm getting scared
at this point,

00:07:02.188 --> 00:07:03.656
I'm hoping it's
just a timing issue,

00:07:03.756 --> 00:07:07.159
of figuring out that throw, and
not an issue with the design.

00:07:07.259 --> 00:07:08.694
That can be big problems.

00:07:15.034 --> 00:07:15.835
Wow.

00:07:18.771 --> 00:07:21.807
 All right, so let's talk
about the design of your weapon.

00:07:21.874 --> 00:07:25.577
The way your blades are
spread out seems a bit wide.

00:07:25.644 --> 00:07:29.348
If this blade were here,
it would be traveling

00:07:29.415 --> 00:07:31.350
forward as opposed to down.

00:07:31.417 --> 00:07:35.688
But I think for me, the biggest
issue is the longer handle is

00:07:35.754 --> 00:07:37.689
really increasing my rotation.

00:07:37.756 --> 00:07:40.193
I do like the shape
of your handle.

00:07:40.293 --> 00:07:42.294
It comes out of the
hand quite nicely.

00:07:42.361 --> 00:07:45.230
And everything still
right and tight.

00:07:45.297 --> 00:07:45.997
Well done.

00:07:46.064 --> 00:07:46.899
 Thank you.

00:07:46.966 --> 00:07:47.867
 All right, gentlemen.

00:07:47.933 --> 00:07:49.602
To test the sharpness
of your blades,

00:07:49.702 --> 00:07:52.705
I'll be throwing them into
our canvas sandbag wall here,

00:07:52.772 --> 00:07:54.040
two times.

00:07:54.140 --> 00:07:55.374
Nate, once again
you're up first.

00:07:55.441 --> 00:07:56.542
You ready?
- I'm ready.

00:08:12.859 --> 00:08:15.628
 So Nate, it punctures the
bag like it's not there.

00:08:15.694 --> 00:08:17.963
I like the positioning
of your blades.

00:08:18.063 --> 00:08:20.099
But what's nice is
the short handle,

00:08:20.165 --> 00:08:24.002
you're going to not have as much
to catch coming over the top

00:08:24.069 --> 00:08:25.037
on rotation.

00:08:25.104 --> 00:08:27.073
That's a big plus in
a throwing weapon.

00:08:27.139 --> 00:08:28.407
Well done, it's a good thrower.

00:08:28.507 --> 00:08:29.909
 Thank you.

00:08:29.976 --> 00:08:30.910
 Richard, you ready?

00:08:31.010 --> 00:08:31.777
 Yes, sir.

00:08:49.828 --> 00:08:51.864
 Again, the positioning
of your blades

00:08:51.931 --> 00:08:53.865
sets it up for a
different rotation

00:08:53.965 --> 00:08:55.901
and I need to adjust
to throw this weapon.

00:08:55.968 --> 00:08:57.770
But it's definitely
a sharp weapon.

00:08:57.836 --> 00:08:59.304
It went right through the bag.

00:08:59.371 --> 00:09:00.071
Good job.

00:09:00.138 --> 00:09:01.641
 Thank you.

00:09:01.741 --> 00:09:05.110
 Nate, Richard, through three
grueling rounds of competition

00:09:05.177 --> 00:09:07.279
you've worked your
britches off to be standing

00:09:07.379 --> 00:09:10.115
right here in this moment.

00:09:10.182 --> 00:09:13.819
And for that we respect
you as craftsman.

00:09:13.885 --> 00:09:15.687
However, in this
arena of competition,

00:09:15.754 --> 00:09:18.523
there can only be one
Forged in Fire Champion.

00:09:18.590 --> 00:09:20.293
Nate, congratulations.

00:09:20.359 --> 00:09:22.294
You are the Forged
in Fire Champion.

00:09:22.361 --> 00:09:25.798
Richard, unfortunately, your
blade did not make the cut.

00:09:25.864 --> 00:09:28.167
 Richard, you brought
us a deadly weapon,

00:09:28.267 --> 00:09:29.669
that was strong and sharp.

00:09:29.769 --> 00:09:32.737
But with that long handle and
the arrangement of your blades,

00:09:32.837 --> 00:09:35.241
it was just harder to control.

00:09:35.308 --> 00:09:36.608
 I understand.

00:09:36.708 --> 00:09:40.379
 Richard please
surrender your weapon.

00:09:40.446 --> 00:09:41.513
 Richard, thank you.

00:09:41.580 --> 00:09:42.914
 The judges made
the right choice.

00:09:43.014 --> 00:09:44.683
I would have made the
same choice myself.

00:09:44.749 --> 00:09:46.719
I have absolutely zero regrets.

00:09:46.819 --> 00:09:50.356
This was a fantastic experience,
the judges are fantastic.

00:09:50.422 --> 00:09:51.923
 Good job, buddy.

00:09:52.023 --> 00:09:53.792
 You know, David, he must be
a brother from another mother.

00:09:53.892 --> 00:09:55.995
I've got a few fashion tips that
I'm going to share with them

00:09:56.095 --> 00:09:57.863
later on before I leave.

00:09:57.963 --> 00:09:59.599
I'm ready to get back to Texas.

00:10:02.201 --> 00:10:03.669
 Nate, congratulations.

00:10:03.769 --> 00:10:05.671
You are the Forged
in Fire Champion,

00:10:05.738 --> 00:10:08.641
and that's a title that comes
with a check for $10,000.

00:10:08.707 --> 00:10:10.176
Good job, brother.

00:10:10.276 --> 00:10:12.544
[clapping]

00:10:12.611 --> 00:10:13.846
 How you feeling right now?

00:10:13.912 --> 00:10:16.081
 I'm feeling great, thank you.

00:10:16.181 --> 00:10:19.085
 Please present your
kpinga it to the judges.

00:10:19.185 --> 00:10:20.185
 I can't believe it.

00:10:20.252 --> 00:10:23.088
Being a full time
bladesmith is my dream.

00:10:23.155 --> 00:10:25.991
That future looks a little
more bright, and that feels--

00:10:26.091 --> 00:10:27.760
wow.

